{
  "description": "start_session derives the new session ID from the request's idempotency key, so resending the same key can never start a second session. Every implementation (TypeScript and Python launchers, the Go terminal UI and its tests) must turn each idempotency_key and harness into session_id, and must reject every invalid key. Hand-written; see agents/cli/TERMINAL_UI_CONTRACT.md.",
  "rule": "The key must be a lowercase, hyphenated UUIDv7 (RFC 9562): 8-4-4-4-12 hex digits, version digit 7, variant digit 8, 9, a, or b. Its first 48 bits are Unix milliseconds, which must lie from 2000-01-01T00:00:00.000Z to 9999-12-31T23:59:59.999Z. session_id is <harness>-<YYYYMMDD>-<HHMMSS>-<hex6>: the UTC date and time of the milliseconds floored to the second, then the first 6 lowercase hex digits of the SHA-256 of the key's 36 ASCII bytes.",
